<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="096" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>UAT round 4 (6-8): an "Email" tab in Word, built from the shared Communication compose components, sends the document as an attachment from the user's own mailbox and files the email against the record; the broken Graph sharing link leaves every Send Email path</title>
    <phase>6 UAT round 3-4 (2026-10-03/04)</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New pane view + tab built from a shared component library, wiring to an existing BFF route that sends mail as the user (OBO), and removal of a failing link path; `.ts`/`.tsx`, build config, possibly `.cs`.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Sends email as the user and attaches a stored document — authorization, data association, a cross-module contract (the Communication module's send route) and a shared-library dependency.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>UAT4-W1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Runs beside 095 (client-only). Disjoint: 096 owns `App.tsx`, `TaskPaneToolbar.tsx`, `TaskPaneNavigation.tsx`, a new `components/views/EmailView.tsx` (+ service), `sendEmailService.ts`, `shareLinkService.ts`, `webpack.config.js`/`tsconfig.json` aliases and their tests; it MUST NOT edit `RelatedToPicker.tsx` or `SaveFlow.tsx` (095's). 096 is the only W1 task allowed to run `dotnet`.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>091, 094</deps>
    <tags>frontend, office-addins, typescript, bff-api, email, communication, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Owner UAT round 4 (2026-10-04), items 6-8, the Send Email failure in the owner's screenshot, and the owner's decisions the same day — including *"for the email form we should use our shared UI components so it looks consistent"*. Record: `notes/042-uat-round4-2026-10-04.md` §1, §3.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer on the Office add-in, the shared Communication component library and the BFF Communication module.</role>

  <goal>In Word, the user writes and sends an email from the pane — using the same compose components as the Spaarke email page — with the current document attached, from their own mailbox, and the sent email is recorded in Spaarke against the same record; no Send Email path depends on a Graph sharing link.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      - **Owner, verbatim (round 4)**: (6) *"Add the send email to the main add-in bar next to 'Find'; could this be an
        email form so do not then have to open Spaarke?"* (7) *"when the email is sent, the email should be associated to
        the same record"* (8) *"the email has this file/document attached"*; and *"for the email form we should use our
        shared UI components so it looks consistent"*. Decisions: send **as the user, from their own mailbox**;
        **Outlook unchanged** (native new-message window) — the in-pane form is Word-only.
      - **Shared compose components (binding — reuse, do not rebuild)**: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/`
        has `EmailRecipients`, `EmailBody`, `EmailComposeActions`, `AttachmentList`, `EmailAssociationsAndTracking`
        (the Spaarke email page's composer pieces; find their consumer, e.g. `src/client/code-pages/CommunicationPage`,
        for how they are assembled). The add-in already resolves `@spaarke/communication-components` by alias for ONE
        file (`tsconfig.json:27`, `webpack.config.js:213` — `logic/connections/provenance`); widen that to the compose
        components (alias + `tsconfig` paths), the way other shared libraries are consumed in this repo. Check each
        component's dependencies before wiring: anything bound to the model-driven host (`Xrm`, `Xrm.WebApi`,
        `window.parent.Xrm`) or to a data service the add-in cannot provide must be fed through props/adapters, not
        copied. React/Fluent version compatibility with the add-in (React 19, Fluent v9) must be confirmed.
      - **The send route already exists**: `POST /api/communications/send` (`Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs:55`,
        `CommunicationAuthorizationFilter`) with `SendCommunicationRequest`: `To`, `Cc`, `Bcc`, `Subject`, `Body`,
        `BodyFormat`, **`SendMode.User`** (OBO, `/me/sendMail`), **`Associations`** (`CommunicationAssociation[]`),
        **`AttachmentDocumentIds`** (sprk_document ids; the server fetches the file and sends a `FileAttachment`; max 150 /
        35 MB), `ArchiveToSpe`. REUSE it — no new send route. Read `CommunicationService` + `EmailChannelSender` to confirm
        what a User-mode send records (the `sprk_communication` row, its associations, the attachment) and what the
        filter demands.
      - **The defect**: Graph refuses `createLink` for SPE container files — *"This sharing scenario is not supported on
        CSP Container site."* (owner screenshot; share-link route `FileAccessEndpoints.cs:118`). Paths that mint a
        document sharing link (`shareLinkService.mintDocumentShareLink`, used by `sendEmailService.ts` for task 086's Word
        choice AND Outlook's native compose) therefore fail.
      - **Word**: replace task 086's Send Email row (above the tabs) with an **Email tab** after Find (Save · To Do · Find
        · Email). The form, from the shared components: To (recipient search showing email — the add-in's contact search
        from task 091 as the data source if the component takes a provider), Cc, Subject (prefilled from the document
        name), Body (prefilled with a short line and the Spaarke **record** link from `openRecordLauncher`, never a
        sharing link), the attachment (the current document's Spaarke file) and the related record. Send ->
        `/api/communications/send` with `SendMode: User`, `AttachmentDocumentIds: [documentId]`, `Associations: [the
        related record]`. After send: a success message with "Open in Spaarke" (the communication) via `openRecord`.
      - **A document not yet in Spaarke** cannot be attached by id: the Email tab says so and offers "Save to Spaarke
        first" (switches to the Save tab).
      - **Outlook**: keep native compose, but its body must stop depending on the sharing link — use the Spaarke
        document/record link instead, so it works again.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-10-04">The email form is built from the shared `Spaarke.Communication.Components` compose components (owner: consistency). A new component in the add-in is allowed only as a thin container that wires them; restyling or re-implementing a shared component is not.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-10-04">Word only for the in-pane form, gated by capability, never `hostType`. Outlook keeps native compose.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-10-04">Send as the user (`SendMode.User`). The sent email is associated with the same record the document is filed to; the document is attached (not linked).</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">No new send route, no second mail sender: reuse `POST /api/communications/send`. A BFF change is allowed only if the existing contract cannot carry what is needed (e.g. the filter refuses the Office caller) — then extend that route minimally and state the placement per CLAUDE.md §10.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">No pane path calls `mintDocumentShareLink` after this task. The share-link route's failure for its other consumer (the Spaarke email composer) is recorded in the note with a recommendation for the main session (owner rule 2026-09-21: findings are fixed in this project).</constraint>
    <constraint source="security">The pane sends only what the user typed and the document/record ids; the server authorizes the send, the attachment read and the association. Never put a token or the BFF URL in a body or URL.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9, semantic tokens, dark mode; accessible labels on every field (as the shared components provide).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests in `shared/**/__tests__/` listed in `ci-gated-suites.txt`; server tests in the existing Communication test classes if the server changes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="parallel wave">Do NOT edit 095's files. Do NOT run `npm run build` (the main session does). Publish size, if the BFF changes, is owed to the main session.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">In Word the tab row is Save · To Do · Find · Email, and task 086's Send Email row above the tabs is gone; in Outlook the tabs are unchanged and Send Email opens native compose.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Email form is composed of the shared `Spaarke.Communication.Components` compose components (recipients, body, attachments, associations, actions) — a test or import check proves the add-in renders those components, not local copies.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The form has To (recipient search showing email, plus free-typed addresses), Cc, Subject prefilled from the document name, Body prefilled with the record link, the attached document shown, and the related record shown.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Send calls `POST /api/communications/send` with `SendMode: User`, `AttachmentDocumentIds: [documentId]` and `Associations` naming the related record; a test asserts the exact request.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">After a successful send: a success message with "Open in Spaarke" for the communication; the form resets.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A document not yet in Spaarke: the Email tab explains and offers "Save to Spaarke first"; Send is not possible.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a refused send (403/400/500) shows the server's reason; nothing is reported as sent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No client code path calls `mintDocumentShareLink`; Outlook's native-compose body carries the Spaarke document/record link instead (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: gated jest green; lint 0; typecheck 0 production; if the BFF changed: build, Communication tests, ArchTests green, CVE clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Live (after deploy): from Word, send an email to yourself — it arrives from your mailbox with the document attached, appears in Sent Items, and the `sprk_communication` row is associated with the record. If unavailable, leave open.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A shared compose component cannot run in the add-in without host-only dependencies (`Xrm`/model-driven services) that props cannot replace, or needs a React/Fluent version the add-in cannot load — STOP and report which component and why; do not copy it.</trigger>
    <trigger>`CommunicationAuthorizationFilter` or the User send mode refuses the Office pane's token (e.g. a missing delegated `Mail.Send` consent on the BFF app) — STOP and report the exact error; consent changes are the owner's.</trigger>
    <trigger>`AttachmentDocumentIds` cannot read an SPE file the user can read, or the attachment limit blocks ordinary documents — report before working around it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read the round-4 note, the shared compose components and their consumer page, the Communication send route/service/sender/filter, 086's and 036's notes, `sendEmailService.ts`, `shareLinkService.ts`, 091's contact search.</step>
    <step>Confirm the components can be consumed (dependencies, versions) and what a User-mode send records (read code; no live send).</step>
    <step>Alias/paths for the shared library; Email tab + thin container over the shared components + send service; tests.</step>
    <step>Remove 086's Send Email row in Word; switch Outlook's body to the Spaarke link; remove `mintDocumentShareLink` from pane paths; tests.</step>
    <step>Record the share-link route defect and recommendation.</step>
    <step>Gates; `notes/096-email-tab.md`; POML status.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>The compose components (`Spaarke.Communication.Components`), `POST /api/communications/send` (send as user, associations, document attachments), 091's contact search, `openRecordLauncher` and the tab shell all exist.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — a thin pane container over shared components and an existing route; the only new surface is the tab and its container, which the owner asked for.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Send Email fails for every user today (Graph refuses sharing links on SPE), and the owner wants to email a document without leaving Word, attached and recorded against the record, looking like the rest of Spaarke.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Email tab (Word)">
      <steps>
        <step>Save a document to a matter; open Email: the same recipient/body/attachment controls as the Spaarke email page; the document chip; the matter shown.</step>
        <step>Send to yourself: it arrives from your mailbox with the .docx attached; the communication record is on the matter.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
    <test name="Outlook unchanged">
      <steps>
        <step>In Outlook, Send Email opens the native new-message window with a working Spaarke link.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

